exports[`getOneRouteDriveBlockerMessage given: [case2b] the approval halt, with a dispute at 70% that owes the human when: [t0] the dispatcher runs with the approval blocker then: the halt a human reads is pinned 1`] = `
"🦉 where were we?

🗿 route.drive
   ├─ where do we go?
   │  ├─ route = <route>
   │  └─ stone = 1.vision
   │
   └─ halted, human approval required
      ├─ 1 dispute owes a human verdict
      │  ├─ verdict: upheld = the driver's call stands · conceded = the reviewer's concern stands
      │  └─ F44 · rename-table · 70%
      │     ├─ ground: wrong · 70%
      │     ├─ holds: limited/i001/blocker.1 · limited/i001/blocker.2 · limited/i001/blocker.9 · limited/i001/nitpick.1 · friendly/i001/nitpick.1
      │     ├─ lean: x
      │     ├─ raised on: 0.prior
      │     └─ read: .fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F44-rename-table.md
      │
      ├─ 1 ruled
      │  └─ F47 · cache-scope · conceded
      │     ├─ ruled on: 2026-11-17
      │     ├─ repair owed: limited/i001/blocker.1 · limited/i001/blocker.2 · limited/i001/blocker.9 · limited/i001/nitpick.1 · friendly/i001/nitpick.1
      │     ├─ next: the driver repairs it in the current diff, then a human approves the stone after it
      │     └─ 🟡 leave the fulcrum file as is; an edit to it reopens the verdict
      │
      ├─ please ask your human to rule on each, then approve once the repair lands
      │  ├─ rhx route.fulcrum.rule --case F44 --as <upheld|conceded>
      │  └─ rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.vision --as approved
      │
      └─ once they do, run
         └─ rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.vision --as passed"
`;

exports[`getOneRouteDriveBlockerMessage given: [case2c] the approval halt, with a corrupt verdict ledger when: [t0] the dispatcher runs with the approval blocker then: the halt a human reads is pinned 1`] = `
"🦉 where were we?

🗿 route.drive
   ├─ where do we go?
   │  ├─ route = <route>
   │  └─ stone = 1.vision
   │
   └─ halted, human approval required
      ├─ the dispute record cannot be read; approval is refused until it is repaired
      │  └─ fulcrum verdict ledger holds an unreadable row at line 1
      │     ├─ ledger: <route>/.route/fulcrum.verdicts.jsonl
      │     ├─ line: {"case": "F44", "ruled": "upheld"
      │     └─ fix: restore the line from git; only rhx route.fulcrum.rule writes this ledger
      │        └─ the ledger sits under the route seal, so a driver needs a human's rhx route.mutate grant allow first
      │
      ├─ first, the driver repairs each fault above; approval is refused until then
      │
      └─ once each fault is repaired, run
         └─ rhx route.drive"
`;

exports[`getOneRouteDriveBlockerMessage given: [case3] feedbackUnabsorbed with an absent taken when: [t0] the dispatcher runs with the feedbackUnabsorbed blocker then: matches snapshot — the held stop, as a driver reads it: stophook - held stop, reply owed 1`] = `
"🦉 the reviewers await your reply

🌕 lets respond
   │
   ├─ review.peer 1/1
   │  ├─ slug = arch
   │  ├─ status = retired from the guard config
   │  ├─ verdict = 2 blockers, 1 nitpick
   │  ├─ absorb from
   │  │  └─ .reviews/peer/1.vision._.review.i001.<hash>.r001._.given.by_peer.arch.md
   │  └─ articulate into
   │     └─ .reviews/peer/1.vision._.review.i001.<hash>.r001._.taken.by_self.arch.md
   │
   ├─ why a retired reviewer still awaits
   │  └─ it spoke, and was then removed from the guard config. what it said
   │     was never answered, and a debt is keyed to the reviewer rather than
   │     to the artifact, so no edit to the artifact can clear it.
   │
   ├─ what to do — answer the retired reviewer
   │  └─ answer it as you would any other — write the .taken above. it will
   │     not speak again, so your answer is what discharges it.
   │
   └─ when you've absorbed this reviewer, run
      └─ rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.vision --as absorbed --that arch"
`;

exports[`getOneRouteDriveBlockerMessage given: [case5] malpartitioned, and a changed file still sits in no partition when: [t0] the dispatcher runs with the malpartitioned blocker then: the bytes a driver reads are pinned 1`] = `
"🦉 the partitions would leave changed files unreviewed — no lane runs until they cover them

🗿 route.guard.partition, on stone 5.1.test
   └─ scope @all
      ├─ 1 changed file sits in no partition
      │  └─ src/route/drive/b.ts → route (+ src/route/drive/**)
      └─ repair — run this, then re-arrive
         └─ rhx route.guard.partition --route .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo --for review --peer @all \\
              --claim 'src/route/drive/**' --into route \\
              --mode apply

✨ did you know?
   ├─ claim each domain whole, in every layer, and the files you edit next stay covered
   └─ e.g. src/route/** and blackbox/{,__snapshots__/}driver.route.* in one partition"
`;
